WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.240
SO IN A YEAR WHEN HALF OF US

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:04.960
FORGOT TO UNMUTE OURSELVES,
WE WERE ALL REMINDED ABOUT THE

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:07.520
IMPORTANCE OF SOUND.
BUT WE STILL ONLY TALK ABOUT

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:09.840
WATCHING A MOVIE.
WE TELL PEOPLE TO GO AND SEE

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:13.440
A MOVIE, BUT THE BEST FILMS ARE
THE ONES WE FEEL, RIGHT HERE.

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:17.200
I HAD THE PRIVILEGE OF BEING TAUGHT
AMERICAN SIGN LANGUAGE FOR MY

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:20.480
ROLE IN "SOUND OF METAL," AND
WHAT I LEARNED FROM JEREMY,

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:23.600
MY SIGN INSTRUCTOR, WAS THAT
TRUE LISTENING AND

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:26.800
TRUE COMMUNICATION GOES FAR
BEYOND WHAT WE HEAR WITH OUR EARS

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:30.080
IT'S SOMETHING WE DO
WITH OUR ENTIRE BODIES.

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:32.800
THE FILMS NOMINATED TONIGHT
FOR BEST SOUND UNDERSTOOD THIS.

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:34.640
THEY MOVED US BEYOND
THEIR SOUNDSCAPES.

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:36.720
THEY SOARED,
EVEN IN THEIR SILENCES.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:38.640
AND THEY STRUCK US AT OUR CORE.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:43.840
HERE ARE THE NOMINEES FOR
ACHIEVEMENT IN SOUND.

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:49.200
“GREYHOUND,” WARREN SHAW,
MICHAEL MINKLER, BEAU BORDERS,

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:50.160
AND DAVID WYMAN.

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:55.760
“MANK,” REN KLYCE,
JEREMY MOLOD,

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:59.760
DAVID PARKER, NATHAN NANCE,
AND DREW KUNIN.

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:06.400
“NEWS OF THE WORLD,” OLIVER
TARNEY, MIKE PRESTWOOD SMITH,

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:08.480
WILLIAM MILLER,
AND JOHN PRITCHETT.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:15.440
“SOUL,” REN KLYCE, COYA ELLIOTT,
AND DAVID PARKER.

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:21.760
“SOUND OF METAL,”
NICOLAS BECKER, JAIME BAKSHT,

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:25.840
MICHELLEE COUTTOLENC,
CARLOS CORTES, AND PHILLIP BLADH.

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:31.720
AND THE OSCAR GOES TO --

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:33.840
“SOUND OF METAL”

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:36.240
[ CHEERS AND APPLAUSE ]

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:46.718
MICHELLEE COUTTOLENC,
CARLOS CORTES, AND PHILLIP BLADH.

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:14.720
SO, THANK YOU SO MUCH FOR THE
ACADEMY, FOR RECOGNIZING THIS
0:02:08.760,1193:02:47.295
NICOLAS BECKER, JAIME BAKSHT,

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:17.680
WONDERFUL FILM.
I'M SORRY, MY ENGLISH IS NOT

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:19.520
VERY GOOD. SO I'M
GOING TO READ A BIT

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:21.840
BECAUSE I DON'T WANT
TO MAKE PROBLEMS.

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:27.040
SO THANK YOU, DARIUS AND ABE, FOR
RECOGNIZING THIS WONDERFUL FILM.

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:31.520
NO, THANK YOU, DARIUS AND ABE, THE
TRUE MASTER BEHIND “SOUND OF METAL.”

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:34.320
THANK YOU SACHA AND BERT
FOR YOUR GREAT SUPPORT.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:38.080
THANK YOU RIZ, PAUL AND OLIVIA
FOR YOUR AMAZING PERFORMANCES

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:39.920
TO MIKKEL FOR HIS COLLABORATION,

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:42.240
TO PHILLIP AND JEREMY
FOR THEIR COMMITMENTS,

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:45.360
TO HEIKKI, KARI, PIETU
ON THEIR CREATIVITY

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:48.240
TO CAROLINA, 
FOR HER BRILLIANCE

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:51.200
TO JAIME, MICHELLEE AND CARLOS,
TOP OF THE NOTCH.

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:54.800
ON BEHALF OF PHILLIP, JAIME
MICHELLEE, CARLOS AND I,

00:02:55.920 --> 00:03:01.520
I THANK YOU ERIC, MICHEL, ROSEANNE,
ROSALINDA, SABINA, DAVID, PABLO, VICTORIA,

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:07.680
CESAR, CHRIS, FANNIE, MARTA, ORLANDO,
BRUNO, CARLA, CONSTANCE, ANTON AND IAN.

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:09.840
WE ARE FIVE ON THE TEAM.
THAT'S WHY IT'S A BIT LONG.

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:12.880
SO, NOW I WOULD LIKE TO SAY
SOMETHING MORE PERSONAL.

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:16.640
FELLINI ONCE SAID, IN THE
HISTORY OF CINEMA,

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:19.520
BEYOND THE EVOLUTION
OF STYLES AND TECHNIQUES

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:23.760
WHAT STAYS EMBODIED IN FILMS
IS THEIR HUMAN VITALITY.

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:28.800
AND WHOEVER ENJOYS IT RECEIVES A
CHARGE OF ENERGY, SOMETHING PULSING

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:33.360
MYSTERIOUS AND VIBRANT.
"SOUND OF METAL" RECEIVED FROM

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:36.400
ITS TEAM SO MUCH CARE,
LOVE, AND ATTENTION.

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:39.680
SO MUCH ENERGY THAT WE BELIEVE
IT'S ONE OF THE REASONS WHY

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:43.600
THE FILM HAS BEEN RECEIVED
BY THE AUDIENCE SO BEAUTIFULLY.

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:45.925
SO, THANK YOU FOR THAT.

00:03:46.334 --> 00:03:47.886
THANK YOU VERY MUCH.

